# Project 3 — Active Learning and Learning-to-Defer

Project 3 studies collaboration between an AI classifier and a simulated human expert.

The experiments use the AG News text classification dataset.

## Baseline AI

The baseline system uses TF-IDF text features together with Logistic Regression to classify news articles into the AG News categories.

The baseline test accuracy is used as a reference for the human-AI collaboration experiments.

## Simulated Expert

A simulated expert is implemented with different reliability levels for different news categories.

This creates an expert that is strong in some areas but weaker in others, rather than assuming a perfect human expert.

## Learning-to-Defer

The learning-to-defer system decides whether the AI should:

- Make the prediction itself, or
- Defer the example to the simulated expert

The evaluation considers both overall team accuracy and the quality of the deferral decisions.

The interface reports values such as:

- Team accuracy
- Deferral rate
- Expert accuracy on deferred examples
- AI accuracy on deferred examples
- AI accuracy on non-deferred examples

## Active Learning

An uncertainty-sampling strategy is used to decide which training examples should be presented to the expert.

This allows the system to learn about expert competence while limiting the number of expert queries.

## Interface and Report

The project includes a dashboard containing the main experimental results and an expert interaction interface.

A PDF report describing the methods, design choices and results is available from the Project 3 interface.

